## Why This Is Asked
- Tests DP state design that tracks both position and budget (flips).
- Requires reconstruction to return exact indices, not just value.

## Key Concepts
- DP state with dual dimension (i, flips)
- Transition depends on current bit; reconstruction via predecessor pointers
- Time/space trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxOnesRun(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const prev = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array.from({length: k+1}, () => null));
  let bestLen = 0, bestEnd = 0, bestJ = 0;
  for (let i=0; i<n; i++) {
    for (let j=0; j<=k; j++) {
      if (s[i] === '1') {
        dp[i][j] = (i>0 ? dp[i-1][j] : 0) + 1;
        prev[i][j] = i>0 ? [i-1, j] : null;
      } else if (j>0) {
        dp[i][j] = (i>0 ? dp[i-1][j-1] : 0) + 1;
        prev[i][j] = i>0 ? [i-1, j-1] : null;
      } else {
        dp[i][j] = 0; prev[i][j] = null;
      }
      if (dp[i][j] > bestLen) { bestLen = dp[i][j]; bestEnd = i; bestJ = j; }
    }
  }
  const start = bestEnd - bestLen + 2;
  return {bestLen, start, end: bestEnd+1, flips: bestJ};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you reduce space to O(k)?
- How would you adapt if flips must happen in blocks?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a 3D DP on a grid with an exact count constraint and path reconstruction, a realistic routing/optimization pattern.

## Key Concepts
- DP on (i,j,t) with 3 dimensions
- Exact-count handling via -inf initialization
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers
- Space optimizations via rolling arrays

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPathWithBoosts(grid, boost, K){
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const neg = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n}, () => Array.from({length:m}, () => Array(K+1).fill(neg)));
  const par = Array.from({length:n}, () => Array.from({length:m}, () => Array(K+1).fill(null)));
  const b00 = boost[0][0] ? 1 : 0;
  dp[0][0][b00] = grid[0][0];
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++){
    for (let j=0;j<m;j++){
      for (let t=0;t<=K;t++){
        const add = boost[i][j] ? 1 : 0;
        if (i===0 && j===0) continue;
        const candFromTop = i>0 ? dp[i-1][j][t - add] : neg;
        const candFromLeft = j>0 ? dp[i][j-1][t - add] : neg;
        const bestPrev = Math.max(candFromTop, candFromLeft);
        if (bestPrev > neg/2) {
          dp[i][j][t] = bestPrev + grid[i][j];
          par[i][j][t] = candFromTop >= candFromLeft ? ['top'] : ['left'];
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // Reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {best: dp[n-1][m-1][K], path: []};
}
```

